WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.310
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm breaking down the amazing new

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.799
Avengers: Infinity War trailer for Marvel
easter eggs and other cool details you might

00:00:08.799 --> 00:00:09.949
have missed.

00:00:09.949 --> 00:00:13.740
If you're here for the first time, I do regular
Marvel videos, and to celebrate the new trailer,

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.200
I'm kicking off a new round of my Infinity
War giveaway for all my subscribers.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.900
Just leave me a comment below about the new
trailer or any requests you have for Infinity

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.900
War videos.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.660
Obviously, speculation and potential spoilers
ahead for Infinity War.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.910
The new trailer introduces more backstory
for Thanos with Gamora revealing her father's

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.120
chilling mission.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.230
"The entire time I knew him, he only ever
had one goal."

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.360
"To wipe out half the universe."

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.890
"If he gets all the infinity stones, he can
do it with the snap of his fingers...

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.489
just like that!"

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:51.170
And that snap is a reference to the classic
Infinity Gauntlet storyline where Thanos literally

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:56.110
snaps his fingers when he's wearing the gauntlet
and half of the universe disappears.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.149
This is an awesome easter egg although we
might not actually get Thanos's exact "snap"

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:02.550
moment in the movie.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:07.240
For example, we may see the Mad Titan's fingers
about to perform that move, followed by a

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.819
sudden cut to black, similar to how at the
end of Avengers: Age of Ultron the camera

00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:20.700
cut before Cap finished the famous comic book
catchphrase, 'Avengers Assemble!'

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.329
"Avengers..."

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:26.299
Thanos's voiceover is as chilling as his mission
and proves that his view of balancing the

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:29.139
universe is a twistedly positive one.

00:01:29.139 --> 00:01:31.380
"The end is near."

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.060
"When I'm done, half of humanity will still
exist."

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:42.389
"Perfectly balanced ... as all things should
be"

00:01:42.389 --> 00:01:44.939
Notice how Thanos is a glass-half-full guy.

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:49.169
He's pointing out half of humanity will still
exist in perfect balance.

00:01:49.169 --> 00:01:54.099
Of course, Thanos will need the time stone,
and we get a terrifying shot of Ebony Maw

00:01:54.099 --> 00:01:55.679
torturing Doctor Strange.

00:01:55.679 --> 00:02:00.419
And it instantly brought to mind this scene
from the comics where Ebony Maw manipulates

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:03.829
Doctor Strange into becoming an unwitting
pawn for Thanos.

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:07.929
Ebony Maw has the ability to deceive even
the strongest of minds and I think we're going

00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:12.980
to see Doctor Strange used by Maw in some
kind of deception against the Avengers.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.610
Thor gets some pretty incredible scenes in
the new trailer.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.370
We see him with Rocket and Groot on the Dwarven
planet Nidavellir, where he's gone in search

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.750
of a new weapon now that he no longer has
his hammer Mjolnir.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:29.280
And we get to see an awesome scene where a
cape-wearing-Thor powers up and harnesses

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.640
either his own lightning powers or the powers
of something else, perhaps an Infinity Stone,

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.640
to create his new weapon.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.530
It's not shown in the trailer, but various
tie-in toys have confirmed that the new weapon

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:44.400
will be Stormbreaker and the handle looks
to be made from wood that Groot donates from

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.400
his own body.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:49.130
Stormbreaker is an axe-like hammer which in
the comics was originally wielded by Beta

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:50.130
Ray Bill.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:54.160
Bill is a popular comic-book character who,
after proving himself worthy enough to wield

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.950
Thor's normally unliftable hammer, was given
the new hammer, Stormbreaker, by Odin.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:03.120
And like Mjolnir, Bill's hammer was created
by the dwarves of Nidavellir.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.220
In the comics, Stormbreaker had the same powers
as Thor's Mjolnir, so it'll be interesting

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.940
to see how Thor uses it in Infinity War and
if there are any differences with his original

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.060
hammer.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.960
In the previous trailer we saw the Black Order
attempt to extract the Mind Stone from Vision's

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.430
forehead, and as I predicted then, the Avengers
have taken Vision to Wakanda to try and safely

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.450
remove it.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:28.890
In this shot, Wakandan high-tech genius Shuri
is using her kimoyo beads to project an image

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.850
of Vision, who you can see lying down at the
bottom of the screen.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:35.950
She looks to be showing this image to Bruce
Banner, whose glasses you can see flash by

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.990
just to the side of the shot.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:41.960
Shuri seems to be working out or actually
even showing Banner how she can extract the

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.760
Mind Stone from Vision while keeping him alive.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:49.470
We know from the Avengers: Infinity War prelude
comic and the Black Panther post-credits scene

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:53.709
that Shuri has developed tech in Wakanda that
removed the HYDRA programming from Bucky's

00:03:53.709 --> 00:03:57.810
brain, so it's not surprising that the Avengers
would call on her again for her brilliance

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:01.680
at inventing and using cutting-edge tech,
this time to try to help Vision.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:06.610
As was hinted at in the first trailer, Bruce
Banner will be getting into Tony's Hulkbuster

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.610
armour.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:12.020
And I really liked this shot of the Hulkbuster
standing tall and Falcon and War Machine flying

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.520
past behind him.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.449
But later it looks like the Hulkbuster might
not be strong enough to withstand the Outrider

00:04:17.449 --> 00:04:20.529
attack as we see him getting overwhelmed.

00:04:20.529 --> 00:04:24.270
If you're worried about Bruce Banner's chances
of survival, well, I think he's probably going

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:28.629
to get out of this one because a recent toy
shows Bruce Banner hulking out while inside

00:04:28.629 --> 00:04:30.330
the Hulkbuster.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.629
Also the first trailer showed a Hulk without
any armour fighting on the Wakandan battlefield.

00:04:34.629 --> 00:04:39.259
Hopefully then an angry Hulk will be able
to take out the Outriders swarming all over

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:40.569
him at this point!

00:04:40.569 --> 00:04:46.229
This flashback shows Thanos and his army conquering
Gamora's people, with the Mad Titan taking

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:49.490
a young Gamora away from her family to raise
as his own.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:53.129
Remember that in the Guardians of the Galaxy
movies, we've seen how Gamora is very much

00:04:53.129 --> 00:04:57.000
Thanos's favourite, which really hurt Nebula
when they were growing up together.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.860
In a recent interview with EW, Josh Brolin
said that although Thanos uses his adoptive

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:07.439
daughter Gamora as a tool for his own gain,
he does feel affection for her and we'll see

00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:11.159
the evolution of their relationship over the
course of the film in flashback scenes like

00:05:11.159 --> 00:05:12.159
this one.

00:05:12.159 --> 00:05:16.120
After all, conquering other places and races,
and taking away some of their youngsters,

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:21.620
was all part of Thanos's grand plan, which
we'll see snap into place in Infinity War.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:26.529
The fact that Gamora is Thanos's favourite
may well mean that, in his eyes, her betrayal

00:05:26.529 --> 00:05:28.900
of all he stands for is simply unbearable.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:32.860
This is one of many reasons I believe the
Mad Titan will sacrifice Gamora by the end

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:33.860
of Infinity War.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:38.130
And I talk about all the clues pointing to
her demise in my new Infinity War Death Theory

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.130
video.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.259
OK, let's talk Iron Man.

00:05:41.259 --> 00:05:46.770
We get to see a bit more of his suit capabilities
when his foot thrusters convert into a supercharged

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:50.830
rocket booster as he zooms up to the circle
of death which we know from previous promos

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.490
has Spider-Man on board.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:57.099
The machine heads out into space and we later
see it smash onto a reddish-orangy-brown coloured

00:05:57.099 --> 00:06:00.430
planet and in the background there's a ton
of wreckage.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:03.630
This planet or moon is Thanos's homeworld
Titan.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:07.789
As well as the flashback scenes with Gamora,
we're likely going to see flashbacks to Thanos's

00:06:07.789 --> 00:06:09.330
earlier life on Titan.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:14.180
Recently, Kevin Feige explained we'll learn
that Titan's population went extinct "because

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.349
of things that [Thanos] thought he could help
prevent, [but] he was not allowed to do [anything

00:06:18.349 --> 00:06:19.349
about them]."

00:06:19.349 --> 00:06:23.289
And after that mass extinction, Thanos "vowed
not to let [it] happen again."

00:06:23.289 --> 00:06:27.560
Now, in the background of the planet there
are various giant objects strewn around which

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.520
are likely left over from Titan's destruction.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.800
In fact, I wonder whether they might be parts
of a giant machine.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:37.600
Remember in Guardians of the Galaxy, the Collector
introduced us to the power of the Infinity

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.059
Stones and we saw a Celestial destroying a
whole planet.

00:06:41.059 --> 00:06:45.389
It might be that something similar happened
on Titan and Celestials attacked Thanos's

00:06:45.389 --> 00:06:46.430
homeworld.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.800
Recently, the Russo Brothers said we should
prepare for a lot of crying in the cinema

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.869
when we watch Avengers: Infinity War and Kevin
Feige has also said we will be getting real

00:06:55.869 --> 00:06:57.120
character deaths.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.639
And in this new trailer, I think we get the
biggest hint that Iron Man might actually

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:02.639
die.

00:07:02.639 --> 00:07:07.279
Listen to Thanos and watch who it cuts back
to.

00:07:07.279 --> 00:07:11.729
Tony's looking pretty beaten down by this
point with his armour broken, and Thanos's

00:07:11.729 --> 00:07:16.469
words obviously echo the fact that Iron Man
kick-started the whole of the Marvel Cinematic

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:17.490
Universe.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:21.619
I also think it's interesting that the Marvel
Studios intro logo was zoomed right in on

00:07:21.619 --> 00:07:26.099
the R when it came on in this trailer and
right there bang in the centre are 2 pictures

00:07:26.099 --> 00:07:30.680
of Tony Stark, a subtle hint perhaps that
he's at the core of this movie?

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:34.879
We've also had all the Soul Stone promo art
teases with Iron Man in the middle of the

00:07:34.879 --> 00:07:39.619
Soul Stone, and I'm getting a feeling Marvel
could want Infinity War to come full circle

00:07:39.619 --> 00:07:42.809
back to the very first movie in the franchise,
Iron Man.

00:07:42.809 --> 00:07:47.279
Robert Downey Jr has said that he wants to
leave on a high, and going out in a blaze

00:07:47.279 --> 00:07:51.150
of glory in Infinity War would definitely
fit that ambition.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:55.809
If Tony Stark really does die, I'm sure there
will be a ton of misty eyes in the theatre.

00:07:55.809 --> 00:08:00.809
Now, the editing in the trailer could, of
course, be a bit of classic misdirection.

00:08:00.809 --> 00:08:04.909
Thanos might be saying this line to someone
else, for example, Spider-Man who we saw getting

00:08:04.909 --> 00:08:10.300
beaten down by Thanos in the first trailer,
or perhaps to Thor or Cap who we also see

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.360
Thanos attack in the new trailer.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:17.080
By the way, even if Iron Man does die, we're
going to see Tony Stark again in Avengers

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:22.309
4 as RDJ's been filming, so we'll either get
flashback scenes or some time-travel shenanigans

00:08:22.309 --> 00:08:26.050
that the remaining Avengers do to try to fix
the events of Infinity War.

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:30.990
So, if Iron Man potentially dying wasn't enough
for you, the trailer actually immediately

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.560
cut to Steve Rogers resisting Thanos and the
gauntlet.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.650
First of all, it's incredible that Cap appears
to be holding Thanos back with just his hands.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:42.970
And that reminds me of how Cap was the only
one who managed to make Mjolnir wobble a little

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:47.020
in Thor's hammer lifting contest in Age of
Ultron, and also of how Cap held on to The

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.460
Winter Soldier's helicopter in Civil War.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:54.030
As for Cap's chances against the Mad Titan,
well, he does have his new shields which are

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:57.280
bound to have some new capabilities we've
not yet seen.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.150
However, notice in this shot that Cap's right
arm is missing its shield, but in this later

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:04.080
shot, the shield is back!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:07.701
This could mean simply that these two shots
in the trailer are shown in a different order

00:09:07.701 --> 00:09:12.210
than they appear in the final movie, or it
might mean that Cap's arm shields are similar

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:16.710
to his triangular shield in the comics, in
other words, part of his shield is used to

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:19.810
protect himself while the other part splits
off to attack a baddie.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:23.620
And I talk in detail about Cap's new shield
in my video on that.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.700
I am still worried for Cap though because
in the Infinity Gauntlet story when Steve

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:32.780
Rogers went up against Thanos, the Mad Titan
easily crushed Captain America's shield and

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.830
then killed him like he was nothing.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:39.180
I'm hoping Cap might hold out better here
but I wouldn't place a bet on his chances

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.430
of survival.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:46.070
OK, on a more upbeat note, I want to appreciate
how awesome this shot of Spidey swinging through

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.010
the floating wreckage of Titan is.

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:52.240
It looks like this scene is from the aftermath
of when Thanos throws a moon at the planet

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:56.410
which was recently released in a still and
I imagine the Avengers might have survived

00:09:56.410 --> 00:10:00.620
this attack perhaps because Doctor Strange
managed to slow down time for himself and

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.230
the other heroes as the moon landed on the
surface.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:07.430
Now, I'd love to hear your thoughts and theories
on the new trailer.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:08.430
What's got you excited?

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:09.920
And who's got you worried?

